# A string operator written as a method suggests the operator (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | where name.contains("x")
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..34
  PIPELINE@0..33
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..33
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      CALL_EXPR@15..33
        FIELD_EXPR@15..28
          NAME_REF@15..19
            IDENT@15..19 "name"
          DOT@19..20 "."
          NAME_REF@20..28
            IDENT@20..28 "contains"
        ARG_LIST@28..33
          L_PAREN@28..29 "("
          LITERAL@29..32
            STRING@29..32 "\"x\""
          R_PAREN@32..33 ")"
  WHITESPACE@33..34 "\n"

error[DS0113]: DataScript has no method calls
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from T | where name.contains("x")
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^ `contains` is called like a method of `name`
  |
  = help: `contains` is an operator that goes between two values: `name contains "x"`
